    "notes": "Inspected all 48 final current source/shared/medium-fi/native-site/fallback views. Exactly three pale fluted columns stand at the mapped southeast corner, with layered bases, two chunky leafy capital rows, corner volutes, concave abaci and both surviving L-shaped entablature returns. Layered fascia/cornice, dentils, coarse relief rhythm and a taller rough broken core distinguish the top. Low mapped remnants leave the destroyed temple interior open. Three ordinary pictures guide proportions; exact damaged carved motifs/inscription letters, individual rubble and repair fittings are simplified or omitted. Same-round corrections trimmed the numeric replacement mask away from the Tabularium and widened the column camera. Source/native whole and entablature views carry complete framing; some synthetic close views intentionally emphasize shafts or low remnants."
